# Topology: multitenant_server — the shared half of the multi-tenant deployment.
#
# One cltl-eliza for every tenant. Its event bus has no tenant configured — the
# stack passes CLTL_TENANT="" — so KombuEventBus binds `cltl.topic.text_in.#`
# and receives every tenant's utterances. Its reply is published with
# `source=event`, which copies the tenant across (Event.with_source), and an
# untenanted bus routes on the *event's* tenant rather than its own
# (cltl-combot/src/cltl/combot/infra/event/kombu.py:107) — so the answer goes back
# to exactly the tenant that asked, and to no other.
#
# `tenant` is declared here rather than in tier-compose.config on purpose. Every
# tier-2 test's probe reads that file; an unexpanded $CLTL_TENANT there would
# reach KombuEventBus as a literal string and bind `cltl.topic.text_out.$CLTL_TENANT`,
# leaving the whole existing suite silently deaf. Two overlays cost two lines and
# no blast radius.
#
# Two settings below look like omissions and are not:
#
#  * `intentions:` stays empty (as in base.config). TopicWorker keeps ONE
#    process-global active flag and never looks at event.metadata.tenant
#    (cltl-combot/src/cltl/combot/infra/topic_worker.py:222-242), so a shared
#    module gated on an intention is switched on and off by whichever tenant
#    spoke last. Ungated is the only correct setting for a module on this side of
#    the boundary today. Pinned by
#    tests/slices/test_intention_routing.py::TestTenantScopedGating.
#  * `topic_intention:`/`topic_desire:` are emptied. Ungated is not enough:
#    ElizaService.start still subscribes to a non-empty intention topic
#    (cltl-eliza/src/cltl_service/eliza/service.py:74-77), which on an untenanted
#    bus means `cltl.topic.intention.#` — every tenant's BDI traffic on one queue.
#    Emptying it also makes the greeting branch unreachable, which matters: that
#    branch publishes Event.for_payload(payload) with NO source (service.py:83-86),
#    so its greeting would be untenanted, routed to the bare `cltl.topic.text_out`
#    key, and delivered to no tenant at all.
#
# cltl-backend is absent for a third reason of the same kind. It is the only
# module that constructs EventLogService, which subscribes to `event_bus.topics`
# when [cltl.event_log.event] is unset — and KombuEventBus.topics unions the
# topics it consumes with the tenant-suffixed routing keys it has *produced on*
# (kombu.py:171-173), so on a shared bus it would subscribe to
# `cltl.topic.text_out.tenant-a` as though that were a topic name.

[cltl.event.kombu]
tenant: $CLTL_TENANT

[cltl.eliza]
intentions:
topic_intention:
topic_desire:
